--
Was KNOWNBUG: N5008 [class.base.init]/9.1 + [class.default.ctor]/3 --
the implicitly defined default constructor of a derived class dropped a
base's default member initializers when the base counted as POD (CBMC's
cpp_is_pod does not model NSDMIs, so no constructor is synthesized for
such a base and the base-initializer loop skipped it).  The synthesized
derived constructor now applies the base's NSDMIs through the flattened
from_base components: a component with its own #default_value is
initialized from it, one whose type transitively carries NSDMIs is
default-constructed; an explicit base initializer WITH arguments
supersedes them, while an empty one (value-initialization, [dcl.init]/8)
still applies them.  Reduced with cvise on cbmc-preprocessed source from
std::optional<std::string> (whose remaining KNOWNBUG is the independent
base-specifier resolution failure).  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.
